  "id": "functional-connectivity-mapping",
  "term": "functional connectivity mapping",
  "definition": "Functional connectivity mapping is a way of identifying and displaying patterns of linked activity across different brain regions. In this packet, it refers to using brain imaging to show a circuit of regions that function together, including areas connected with the mesolimbic reward pathway.",
